Title: Jekyll & Hyde
Credit: written by
Author: Liam Dunstan



INT. DR. JEKYLL'S HOME (BASEMENT) - NIGHT

Dr. Jekyll opens the basement door, a dark descending stair case into a pitch black space. Dr. Jekyll slowly walks down the stair case, finding the light switch on the wall at the base of the stairs. 

A single light bulb hangs from the roof and illuminates the room. Jekyll looks around the room, an archaic wooden chair sits in the corner of the room, an old circuit box resides beside it. Dr. Jekyll stares at the chair for a slight second. He walks back up the stairs. 

Dr. Jekyll returns to the basement with a box of items. He places the box by the stairs. He pulls the chair into the center of the room, before taking out a leather belt and measuring his wrist alongside the chair's arm. He grabs a knife and makes a hole for the buckle prong. He grabs out a second belt out to do the same. 

Dr. Jekyll pulls out wires from the box, he attaches them to the side of the chair with suction pads at the end. He connects the wires to the circuit box, and places a switch beside the chair. 

Cut to later:

Dr. Jekyll, dressed down in a singlet and dress pants, stands away from the chair as it stares back at him. In his hand is a syringe. He places himself into the chair forcefully as if someone else is forcing him. 

Jekyll attaches the suction cups to his temple. Places a leather belt in between his teeth. He straps his left hand in. 

He stops, takes a deep breath. 

He injects himself with his serum, before quickly strapping in his other arm, and flicking the switch. 

The electricity surges through Jekyll. The light flickers and burns out quickly. 

INT. DR. JEKYLL'S HOME (BASEMENT) - NIGHT

Hyde opens his eyes for the first time. His body lifts from the ground like a corpse rising from the dead in the darkness of the basement. 

Hyde moves up the stairs towards the light of the kitchen, each steps louder than the last as the wood creaks under Hyde's new weight. The light illuminates his newfound features, and he examines his body as he walks up the stairs. The skin on his hand is tighter, and the paper cuts are gone. His forearms are scar-less. 

As Hyde enters into the light, his new form becomes clearer. He is physically taller, more muscular, his hair a dark brown, and his eyes wider. Hyde feels over his face familiarizing himself with the smoothness, the folds of age now absent. 
